# ---------------- Abstract ----------------
H('Abstract')
P('The ten families of mobilised colistin resistance (mcr) genes encode phosphoethanolamine transferases that are structurally and functionally equivalent to chromosomal EptA. Where each family came from, and which chromosomal genes might be recruited next, remain only partly resolved. We assembled 150 chromosomal phosphoethanolamine transferases from RefSeq, drawn from 44 genus-level lineages of Enterobacterales and from candidate donor taxa outside the order, and analysed them together with reference alleles of MCR-1 to MCR-10 and MCR-12. Maximum-likelihood phylogeny under the LG model placed every mobilised protein inside a single clade of 76 sequences that also contains chromosomal EptA of Escherichia coli, while the paralogous EptB and CptA/EptC clades were recovered as separate, well-supported groups. The mobilised proteins were not monophyletic within that clade. Each family instead grouped with a different chromosomal relative, and the identity to the closest chromosomal protein ranged from 41.0% for MCR-12 to 99.0% for MCR-9. The catalytic threonine, the metal-coordinating glutamate, histidine and aspartate residues and the three disulfide-forming cysteine pairs were invariant across all 161 proteins, and marginal ancestral reconstruction recovered the complete catalytic set at every node subtending a mobilised family, with posterior probabilities of 1.00. Codon-based estimates gave dN/dS values of 0.08 to 0.35 between families and 0.10 to 0.32 between each mobilised gene and its chromosomal progenitor. Insertion sequences or transposases flanked the mobilised copies in five of the six loci with informative annotation, whereas no transposase profile was detected within 9 kb of four chromosomal donor genes. Eight chromosomal proteins shared at least 60% identity with a mobilised family, and these, together with the wider EptA clade in Aeromonas, Shewanella, Buttiauxella, Vibrio and Moraxellaceae, constitute the most plausible source of further mobilisation events.',indent=False)
P('',indent=False)
RICH([('Keywords: ',False),('mcr',True),(', colistin resistance, phosphoethanolamine transferase, ',False),('eptA',True),(', comparative genomics, horizontal gene transfer, One Health',False)],indent=False)
