# ---------------- Introduction ----------------
H('1. Introduction')
RICH([('Colistin returned to clinical use because there was little else left. Decades after it had been abandoned on grounds of nephrotoxicity, the spread of carbapenem-resistant ',False),('Enterobacterales',True),(' forced clinicians back onto polymyxins for infections that no longer responded to anything else (Poirel et al., 2017). Resistance to colistin was, for a long time, thought to arise only through chromosomal mutation, most often in the two-component regulators that control lipid A modification. That assumption ended with the description of ',False),('mcr-1',True),(' on a conjugative plasmid from a Chinese pig isolate (Liu et al., 2016). Within three years, nine further families had been reported from humans, food animals and the environment on four continents, and the gene is now a standing feature of surveillance programmes worldwide.',False)])
RICH([('All ',False),('mcr',True),(' products belong to the alkaline phosphatase superfamily and act as phosphoethanolamine transferases. They attach a phosphoethanolamine group to the 1 and 4′ phosphates of lipid A, which lowers the net negative charge of the outer membrane and weakens the electrostatic attraction that polymyxins depend on. The same chemistry is performed by chromosomal enzymes that long predate the clinical use of colistin. ',False),('Escherichia coli',True),(' carries three of them. EptA modifies lipid A under PmrAB control, EptB transfers phosphoethanolamine to the outer Kdo residue of the inner core (Reynolds et al., 2005), and CptA, also called EptC, modifies the heptose I phosphate. ',False),('Neisseria meningitidis',True),(' LptA and ',False),('Campylobacter jejuni',True),(' EptC perform related reactions and contribute to intrinsic resistance against cationic antimicrobial peptides (Tzeng et al., 2005; Cullen et al., 2011; Wanty et al., 2013).',False)])
RICH([('Structural work on MCR-1 showed how close that relationship is. The periplasmic domain adopts the alkaline phosphatase fold, binds zinc, and uses a threonine nucleophile that becomes transiently phosphorylated during catalysis (Hu et al., 2016; Ma et al., 2016; Coates et al., 2017). The same fold, the same metal site and the same nucleophile are present in ',False),('N. meningitidis',True),(' LptA, whose structure was solved years before ',False),('mcr-1',True),(' was found (Wanty et al., 2013). Mobilisation therefore did not require a new enzyme. It required a route out of a chromosome, and insertion sequences supplied it. ISApl1 brackets ',False),('mcr-1',True),(' in a composite transposon designated Tn6330, and the element is progressively lost once the gene has settled on a stable plasmid backbone (Snesrud et al., 2016; Poirel et al., 2017; Snesrud et al., 2018).',False)])
RICH([('Individual donor taxa have been proposed for several families. ',False),('Moraxella',True),(' species carry chromosomal genes that resemble ',False),('mcr-1',True),(' and ',False),('mcr-2',True),(' closely enough to be regarded as their probable origin (AbuOun et al., 2017; Kieffer et al., 2017), and ',False),('mcr-4',True),(' was noted on discovery to resemble a chromosomal protein of ',False),('Shewanella frigidimarina',True),(' (Carattoli et al., 2017). These observations were made family by family, using whatever comparisons were available at the time. What has not been done is to place all ten families in one phylogeny with a taxonomically balanced set of chromosomal homologues, and then ask, with the same evidence, three questions in sequence. Do the mobilised genes share a single origin or many? Which chromosomal lineage sits closest to each of them? And which chromosomal genes have the properties that would make them plausible candidates for the next mobilisation event?',False)])
RICH([('This study addresses those questions. Chromosomal phosphoethanolamine transferases were retrieved across the breadth of the ',False),('Enterobacterales',True),(' and from the taxa implicated as donors, analysed together with the reference alleles of every named ',False),('mcr',True),(' family, and examined for phylogenetic placement, domain architecture, active-site conservation, ancestral state, selective regime, base composition and genomic context.',False)])

# ---------------- Methods ----------------
H('2. Materials and Methods')
H('2.1. Reference alleles of mobilised colistin resistance genes',3)
RICH([('Nucleotide sequences for the reference allele of each ',False),('mcr',True),(' family were taken from the NCBI Bacterial Antimicrobial Resistance Reference Gene Catalog (Feldgarden et al., 2021), as distributed with ABRicate v1.0.1 (https://github.com/tseemann/abricate). The catalogue provided ',False),('mcr-1.1',True),(' (NG_050417.1), ',False),('mcr-2.1',True),(' (NG_051171.1), ',False),('mcr-3.1',True),(' (NG_055505.1), ',False),('mcr-4.1',True),(' (NG_057470.1), ',False),('mcr-5.1',True),(' (NG_055658.1), ',False),('mcr-6.1',True),(' (NG_055781.1), ',False),('mcr-7.1',True),(' (NG_056413.1), ',False),('mcr-8.1',True),(' (NG_061399.1), ',False),('mcr-10.1',True),(' (NG_066767.1) and ',False),('mcr-12.1',True),(' (NG_245195.1). The ',False),('mcr-9.1',True),(' allele (MK070339) was taken from the ResFinder database distributed with the same package. All 116 catalogued ',False),('mcr',True),(' alleles were retained for the analysis of base composition. Coding sequences were translated with the bacterial genetic code in Biopython v1.88 (Cock et al., 2009); every reference allele yielded a single open reading frame with one terminal stop codon and no internal stop.',False)])
H('2.2. Chromosomal phosphoethanolamine transferases',3)
RICH([('Candidate chromosomal homologues were retrieved from the NCBI RefSeq non-redundant protein collection (O’Leary et al., 2016) through the Entrez programming interface. For each of 35 genus-level taxa of ',False),('Enterobacterales',True),(' and for ten taxa outside the order that have been implicated as donors or that carry well-characterised paralogues (',False),('Moraxella',True),(', ',False),('Aeromonas',True),(', ',False),('Shewanella',True),(', ',False),('Vibrio',True),(', ',False),('Acinetobacter',True),(', ',False),('Neisseria',True),(', ',False),('Campylobacter',True),(', ',False),('Cupriavidus',True),(', ',False),('Pseudomonas',True),(' and ',False),('Burkholderia',True),('), proteins annotated as phosphoethanolamine transferases or as ',False),('eptA',True),(', ',False),('eptB',True),(', ',False),('eptC',True),(' or ',False),('cptA',True),(' gene products and between 400 and 700 residues in length were collected. The EptA, EptB and EptC proteins of ',False),('E. coli',True),(' K-12 MG1655 (NP_418538.2, NP_418002.2 and NP_418390.1) were added as anchors. The 353 retrieved proteins were dereplicated by greedy clustering on shared 4-mers at a Jaccard threshold of 0.5, which corresponds to approximately 80% identity, and one representative per cluster was retained; additional representatives were kept for the donor genera. The final working set contained 150 chromosomal proteins and 11 mobilised proteins, 161 in total. Accessions, organisms and lengths are listed in Supplementary Table S1.',False)])
H('2.3. Alignment and phylogenetic inference',3)
P('Protein sequences were aligned with FAMSA (Deorowicz et al., 2016) as implemented in pyfamsa v0.7.0, giving an alignment of 808 columns. Poorly aligned positions were removed with trimAl (Capella-Gutiérrez et al., 2009) in pytrimal v0.8.5 under the automated1 heuristic, leaving 313 columns. A maximum-likelihood tree was inferred from the trimmed alignment with VeryFastTree v4.0.4 (Piñeiro et al., 2020), a vectorised implementation of FastTree 2 (Price et al., 2010), under the LG substitution model (Le & Gascuel, 2008) with the CAT approximation and subsequent Gamma20 rescaling; the fitted shape parameter was 1.385. Branch support was estimated from 100 non-parametric bootstrap replicates generated by resampling alignment columns, each analysed under the same model, and bipartition frequencies were mapped onto the maximum-likelihood topology with DendroPy v5.1.0. The tree was rooted at its midpoint. Clades were delimited by expanding outward from each of the three E. coli anchors until a node was reached that contained another anchor.',indent=False)
H('2.4. Sequence identity, domain architecture and active-site mapping',3)
P('Pairwise amino acid identity was calculated over columns at which both sequences carried a residue in the untrimmed alignment. Hydropathy was computed on the Kyte and Doolittle scale over a sliding window of 19 residues, and contiguous segments of at least 17 residues with a mean value above 1.6 were merged and counted as predicted membrane-spanning segments. Residues reported from the MCR-1 crystal structures as catalytic, metal-coordinating or disulfide-forming (Hu et al., 2016; Ma et al., 2016; Coates et al., 2017; Zhao et al., 2018) were located in MCR-1.1, mapped to alignment columns, and their occupancy was tabulated separately for the mobilised proteins, for the chromosomal members of the EptA clade and for the full chromosomal set. Positional conservation was summarised as one minus the Shannon entropy of each column normalised by log2(20), computed only for columns with residues in at least 40% of the sequences of a group.',indent=False)
H('2.5. Ancestral sequence reconstruction',3)
P('Marginal ancestral states were reconstructed on the untrimmed alignment under the LG model with empirical equilibrium frequencies and four discrete gamma rate categories with a shape parameter of 1.385, using the rooted maximum-likelihood topology and its branch lengths. Conditional likelihoods were obtained by Felsenstein pruning, combined with the complementary likelihoods of the rest of the tree, and averaged over rate categories weighted by the per-site likelihood of each category. Exchangeabilities and equilibrium frequencies for the LG matrix were taken from the pyvolve v1.1.0 distribution. Nodes subtending each mobilised family and its closest chromosomal relatives were selected for reporting.',indent=False)
H('2.6. Selection and base composition',3)
RICH([('Codon alignments were generated by threading the coding sequences onto the corresponding protein alignments. Numbers of synonymous and non-synonymous substitutions per site were estimated by the counting method of Nei and Gojobori (1986) as implemented in Biopython. Pairs for which the estimator did not converge, which occurs when synonymous divergence is saturated, were excluded and are reported as such. Comparisons were made between the reference alleles of different ',False),('mcr',True),(' families and between each mobilised gene and the coding sequence of its closest chromosomal relative. G+C content was computed over whole coding sequences and at third codon positions.',False)])
H('2.7. Genomic context and detection of mobile elements',3)
RICH([('Genomic context was examined for the original deposits of ',False),('mcr-1',True),(' (KP347127), ',False),('mcr-2',True),(' (LT598652), ',False),('mcr-3',True),(' (KY924928), ',False),('mcr-4',True),(' (MF543359), ',False),('mcr-5',True),(' (KY807921), ',False),('mcr-7.1',True),(' (MG267386) and ',False),('mcr-8',True),(' (MG736312), and for the chromosomal donor loci. Annotated flat files and sequence were retrieved from the European Nucleotide Archive, and coding features within 8 to 9 kb of the transferase gene were extracted. For chromosomal loci without deposited annotation, open reading frames of at least 120 codons were predicted in all six frames within 9 kb of the gene and searched against the 266 transposase profile hidden Markov models distributed with ISEScan (https://github.com/xiezhq/ISEScan) using pyhmmer v0.12.3 at an E-value threshold of 1 × 10⁻⁵.',False)])
H('2.8. Data and code availability',3)
P('All sequences analysed are public records held by NCBI and the European Nucleotide Archive and are identified by accession in Supplementary Table S1. Alignments, the maximum-likelihood tree with bootstrap support, bootstrap replicate trees, reconstructed ancestral states and the analysis scripts accompany this article as supplementary files.',indent=False)

